The project information platform moves from Docuvault to Corvantis on Novem=
ber 28. The migration scope memo is attached and I need everyone to read th=
e second page rather than the summary.<br />
<br />
What migrates: all drawing files, specifications, final submittals, execute=
d contracts and the project directory, for every project regardless of age.=
<br />
<br />
What does not migrate: project correspondence, meeting minutes, transmittal=
s, RFI and ASI logs, and markups, for any project whose last activity preda=
tes January 1, 2014. The legacy correspondence store is structured in a way=
 Corvantis cannot ingest and the vendor quoted a remediation cost we did no=
t approve.<br />
<br />
If you have a closed project from before 2014 whose correspondence you beli=
eve is load bearing, tell me before November 21 and we will handle it indiv=
idually. Docuvault stays available read-only through 2018 and is then decom=
missioned.
